{% doc %}
  Renders a small interface icon as inline SVG, drawn from the outlines of the icon font the theme used before
  (same 512-unit em box), so it keeps the old glyph's size and position: 1em square, sitting 1/16em below the
  baseline, painted in currentColor. The wrapper is an <i> so existing "button i" rules keep applying.
  assets/storefront.js builds the arrow-up icon with the same markup for the back-to-top button.

  @param {string} icon - One of 'search', 'close', 'user', 'arrow-up'.

  @example
  {% render 'theme-icon', icon: 'search' %}
{% enddoc %}
